Emerging Healthcare Trends Shaping the Dry Eye Disease Market
In 2025, the Dry Eye Disease market is being reshaped by several converging healthcare and lifestyle trends. One of the most influential is the surge in digital eye strain, driven by prolonged screen exposure across work, education, and personal life. This has expanded the patient base beyond the elderly to include younger, digitally active populations.
Another key trend is the transition toward disease-modifying therapies, supported by advances in ocular surface science and drug formulation. Ophthalmology practices are increasingly adopting structured diagnostic protocols to classify disease severity and guide targeted treatment. In parallel, digital health platforms and e-pharmacies are improving treatment continuity by enabling prescription refills, patient education, and long-term therapy adherence.

Key Market Drivers Accelerating Industry Growth
Several structural drivers continue to support sustained growth in the Dry Eye Disease market:
•	Aging global population, leading to higher prevalence of tear film dysfunction
•	Rising digital device use, increasing incidence of chronic and lifestyle-induced dry eye
•	Clinical advances in anti-inflammatory therapies, improving long-term disease control
•	Improved diagnostic awareness among eye care professionals, supporting early intervention
•	Expansion of online pharmacies, enhancing access to prescription treatments
Collectively, these factors reinforce dry eye disease as a long-term therapeutic area with recurring treatment demand.

